# Maps git author names onto one identity per person.
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS
# Ako's commits are split across two author names, "AkoBaloyi" and "Ako Baloyi", both from the
# same email address. git shortlog therefore reports four contributors for a team of three,
# which misrepresents the contribution split in a submission that is partly marked on
# contribution. The real split is Ako 37, Zubuhle 21, Kyuri 7.
#
# A mailmap fixes the reporting without rewriting any commit. History is untouched; git simply
# canonicalises the name when it reports. Rewriting history to fix a display name would have
# changed every commit hash on every branch for all three of us, which is a far worse trade.
#
# Applies to git shortlog, git log and git blame automatically.

Ako Baloyi <Akobaloyi01@gmail.com> AkoBaloyi <Akobaloyi01@gmail.com>
Zubuhle Nel <Zubuhle01@gmail.com> Za <Zubuhle01@gmail.com>
Kyuri Reddy <kyuri.reddy@gmail.com> Kyuri <kyuri.reddy@gmail.com>
